      "markdownBody": "# CodeRabbit findings for PAN-5107 (PR #5109)\n\nCodeRabbit posted 4 inline finding(s). CodeRabbit is advisory: nothing waits for these,\nbut each one gets an answer, either a fix or a reply with your reason.\n\n- Thread 4526592329 · apps/mobile/README.md:239 [Minor]: Fix the revoke-skip rationale. It holds only for the `requested` outcome.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5109#discussion_r4526592329\n- Thread 4526592381 · apps/mobile/src/shell/SettingsScreen.tsx:244 [Minor]: Fix punctuation in the error message.\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5109#discussion_r4526592381\n- Thread 4526592393 · changelog.mdx:20 [Minor]: Correct the trigger for \"Delete on the web\".\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5109#discussion_r4526592393\n- Thread 4526592405 · configuration/phone.mdx:170 [Minor]: Correct the failure condition for \"Delete on the web\".\n  https://github.com/eltmon/overdeck/pull/5109#discussion_r4526592405\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Read each thread (open its link, or the code at the path and line).\n2. If you agree with a finding, fix it.\n3. If you reject a finding, reply on its thread with your reason:\n   `gh api repos/eltmon/overdeck/pulls/5109/comments/<thread id>/replies -f body=\"<reason>\"`\n4. If you changed code: run the quality gates on what you touched, commit, push, then run `pan review request PAN-5107`.\n   If you only replied, you are done.\n5. If PR #5109 has already merged when you read this, nothing more lands on it: open a follow-up issue\n   for the findings you agree with instead of pushing."
